  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "When Fallen Flower Hall descends on green ghost desert she steps out first for Fang clan, greets Suan Bu Jin, and says she represents the clan both to thank him and to start cooperation. She invites him inside for seven li fragrant tea and presses a deal around impermanence rocks. She often handles external affairs and has experience dealing with forces and experts.",
      "chapters": [
        1513
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_fallen_flower_hall",
        "fac_fang_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She has an ordinary appearance. She is a bit fat, but her smile is amiable and she gives off a warm feeling.",
      "chapters": [
        1513
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "A purple tongue sword hits her, stiffens her, and turns her face purple. Fang Yun and Fang Leng slow the sword with Fallen Flower Hall’s light while vines and flower petals try to heal her. Fang Yuan uses the strike to weaken Fang clan after she had planned to use him during the fight. Third supreme elder Fang Hua Sheng’s orange light from Chicken Dog Coop saves her life, but she stays unconscious and is sent back to Fang clan headquarters.",
      "chapters": [
        1519
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "purple-tongue-wound",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yun",
        "char_fang_leng",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_fang_hua_sheng",
        "house_chicken_dog_coop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Di Chang later recalls that she and Fang Yuan had fought Divine Bean Palace when it could only charge without killer moves.",
      "chapters": [
        1523
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "purple-tongue-wound",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_di_chang",
        "house_divine_bean_palace"
      ]
    }
  ],
